claim.claim-text:
a surface vessel (12);
a tubular tendon (52) extending between the surface vessel (12) and a lower connection system (190) disposed at a seabed (5), the tubular tendon (52) coupled to the surface vessel (12) with an upper connection system (100); and
an electrical cable (56) extending through a central passage (54) of the tubular tendon (52) and configured to heat sea water in the central passage (54) of the tubular tendon (52);
a cooling system (160, 180) comprising:

a cooling joint (162) disposed subsea along the tubular tendon (52), wherein the cooling joint (162) includes a vent (164) and a port (162P) positioned above the vent (164);
a seal assembly (166) positioned along the central passage (54) within the cooling joint (162) above the vent (164), wherein the seal assembly (166) extends radially from the electrical cable (56) to the cooling joint (162), wherein the seal assembly (166) is configured to prevent the flow of sea water through the central passage (54) of the tubular tendon (52) between a first portion of the central passage (54) below the seal assembly (166) and a second portion of the central passage (54) above the seal assembly (166);
wherein the vent (164) is configured to vent sea water flowing upward through the first portion of the central passage (54) of the tubular tendon (52) via natural convection and allow cooling of the electrical cable (56) extending through the first portion of the central passage (54);
a pump (132, 172) configured to pump sea water through the port (162P) and along a flowpath (176, 186) into and up the central passage (54) of the tubular tendon (52) to cool the electrical cable (56) extending through the second portion of the central passage (54).

a foundation (194) extending into the seabed (5), wherein the foundation (194) is coupled to a lower end of the tubular tendon (52);
a J-tube (196) coupled to and extending from the tubular tendon (52); and
a bell-mouth (198) coupled to an end of the J-tube (196);
wherein the electrical cable (56) extends from the tubular tendon (52) and through the J-tube (196).
